# Invoice / quote contact line layout

## Learned 2026-09-14 (Blue Whale Construction invoice)

Customer fixture (Bill To):

- **BLUE WHALE Construction**
- ABN: 38 629 116 856
- 1/15 Parramatta RD, Underwood QLD 4119
- Phone: **0412 473 160**
- Email: **office@bluewhaleconstruction.com.au**

Owner feedback on the PDF/email attachment: contact looked awkward — phone appeared split (e.g. `0412 473 16` on one line, `0|office@…` on the next) because phone and email were forced onto **one** line with a `|` separator in a narrow column.

## Cause (was)

`InvoiceTemplate` / `QuoteTemplate` used inline `phone | email` on one `<p>`. PDF/print in a narrow column wrapped mid-number (e.g. Blue Whale `0412 473 16` / `0|office@…`).

## Preferred layout (owner) — applied in templates

1. **Phone alone** on its own line (`whitespace-nowrap`).
2. **Email** on the next line (`break-all` OK for long addresses).
3. No `|` joining them. Same for company header + Bill To / Quote To in **InvoiceTemplate** and **QuoteTemplate**.

## Do

- Keep stacked phone/email lines in invoice/quote HTML → PDF paths.
- Sister paths (`lib/pdf/serverReceiptPdf`, shipping PDF) still use `phone | email` for Selpic footer — change only if the same wrap shows up there.

## Do not

- Reintroduce single-line `phone | email` on invoice/quote customer or company blocks.
- Fix only one customer fixture — any long phone + long email hits the same bug.
